WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:03.670
Earlier this year, we covered a story out of Sanger, Texas

2
00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:06.138
about a grocery store built inside of a high school

3
00:00:06.138 --> 00:00:08.340
with a surprising twist.

4
00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:09.700
They don't accept money.

5
00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:12.867
The only currency they use is good deeds.

6
00:00:12.867 --> 00:00:16.620
We were so inspired by this story that we wanted to

7
00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:21.620
do a follow-up and we may have a follow-up on that follow-up

8
00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:24.150
and some more surprise twists in store,

9
00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:26.520
but first take a look.

10
00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:28.330
Anthony Love the principal of

11
00:00:28.330 --> 00:00:29.812
Linda Tutt High School joins us

12
00:00:29.812 --> 00:00:32.310
now I'm very excited to meet him.

13
00:00:32.310 --> 00:00:33.570
Welcome Anthony.

14
00:00:33.570 --> 00:00:37.133
You have your students pay with good deeds.

15
00:00:38.443 --> 00:00:41.640
What's your advice on what good deeds are?

16
00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:44.420
That could be going above and beyond in the classroom.

17
00:00:44.420 --> 00:00:46.900
That could be being a positive mentor

18
00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:48.590
or just a friend to another student

19
00:00:48.590 --> 00:00:50.100
who's having a hard time.

20
00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:52.693
There is no limit for the possibilities

21
00:00:52.693 --> 00:00:57.693
or ways that schools can have a program like this.

22
00:00:57.700 --> 00:01:01.600
We, here at the show, would just love to get involved.

23
00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:05.950
I'm so personally inspired by what you are doing.

24
00:01:05.950 --> 00:01:10.098
I do see endless possibilities for your program.

25
00:01:10.098 --> 00:01:11.120
(audience clapping)

26
00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:13.820
And here we are back with us again.

27
00:01:13.820 --> 00:01:16.166
It's Principal Anthony Love.

28
00:01:16.166 --> 00:01:17.842
(audience clapping)

29
00:01:17.842 --> 00:01:18.804
Hello

30
00:01:18.804 --> 00:01:20.190
Hi Principal Love

31
00:01:20.190 --> 00:01:21.460
How is everything going?

32
00:01:21.460 --> 00:01:22.930
What's the latest and greatest

33
00:01:22.930 --> 00:01:25.800
with your high school grocery store paid with good deeds?

34
00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:29.156
So the store has been great, students.

35
00:01:29.156 --> 00:01:33.710
All the time students want to volunteer or

36
00:01:33.710 --> 00:01:35.582
be a part of it somehow.

37
00:01:35.582 --> 00:01:38.440 line:15%
Up-to-date, we've been able to help close

38
00:01:38.440 --> 00:01:43.110 line:15%
to 350 families, which comes out to a little more

39
00:01:43.110 --> 00:01:45.260 line:15%
than 15 hundred people

40
00:01:45.260 --> 00:01:46.860
that we've been able to help

41
00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:49.083
with food insecurities.

42
00:01:50.090 --> 00:01:51.890 line:15%
That's what I was going to say as much

43
00:01:51.890 --> 00:01:54.300 line:15%
as this is such a poetic, lofty

44
00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:57.960 line:15%
brilliant way to bring out the best in people.

45
00:01:57.960 --> 00:02:00.840
You're also helping people who are food insecure.

46
00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:03.580
I think what you're doing is game-changing in every way.

47
00:02:03.580 --> 00:02:05.980
And when you were last here, you told us

48
00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:07.100
that you wanted to see

49
00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:09.140
good deed grocery stores replicated

50
00:02:09.140 --> 00:02:12.240
in other school districts and Delay Middle School

51
00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:15.060
in Lewisville, Texas heard about your story

52
00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:17.530
and they wanted to follow in your footsteps.

53
00:02:17.530 --> 00:02:20.861
And we have the Delay Middle School principal here

54
00:02:20.861 --> 00:02:24.182
Charde Dockery, Principal Dockery.

55
00:02:24.182 --> 00:02:25.015
Hi

56
00:02:25.015 --> 00:02:26.377
(audience clapping)

57
00:02:26.377 --> 00:02:29.550
Principal Dockery I'm so happy to meet you.

58
00:02:29.550 --> 00:02:34.210
How do you think that a good deed grocery store could work

59
00:02:34.210 --> 00:02:36.620
and benefit inside of your school?

60
00:02:36.620 --> 00:02:38.550
Oh, wow. So Delay Middle School,

61
00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:41.961 line:15%
we're about 90% economically disadvantaged,

62
00:02:41.961 --> 00:02:43.690 line:15%
which means most of our students

63
00:02:43.690 --> 00:02:45.440 line:15%
receive free reduced lunch.

64
00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:49.110 line:15%
A lot of our families are living in low-income housing.

65
00:02:49.110 --> 00:02:52.730 line:15%
From a trailer home communities to budget suites, and some

66
00:02:52.730 --> 00:02:53.910 line:15%
of them are actually homeless.

67
00:02:53.910 --> 00:02:58.330
So they do not have access to just kind of fresh organic

68
00:02:58.330 --> 00:03:01.752
or healthy foods just within their

69
00:03:01.752 --> 00:03:04.520
immediate community.

70
00:03:04.520 --> 00:03:07.660
And I just, I saw Principal Love's story,

71
00:03:07.660 --> 00:03:11.330
and even the pieces on kindness and

72
00:03:11.330 --> 00:03:14.325
empathy and just servant leadership.

73
00:03:14.325 --> 00:03:17.610
Our students definitely need that experience

74
00:03:17.610 --> 00:03:19.972
because they do not have those experiences

75
00:03:19.972 --> 00:03:22.532
in their communities and they don't travel outside

76
00:03:22.532 --> 00:03:25.630
of their two mile radius, often.

77
00:03:25.630 --> 00:03:27.660
Principal Love,

78
00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:29.810
Do you have any advice,

79
00:03:29.810 --> 00:03:32.623
may I ask, since you've done it?

80
00:03:33.510 --> 00:03:36.310
So you got to have a champion for the grocery store.

81
00:03:36.310 --> 00:03:39.100
You gotta have somebody who believes in it

82
00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:41.556
sees the vision and you just have to have

83
00:03:41.556 --> 00:03:46.160
the mindset that failure is not an option.

84
00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:49.550
There'll be things come up that you're not expecting

85
00:03:49.550 --> 00:03:52.310
but you just have to have a team with you that is there

86
00:03:52.310 --> 00:03:55.360
to support you and to support the students.

87
00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:59.690
Hmm. That sounds like really honest

88
00:03:59.690 --> 00:04:03.750
and real world advice, find the right people

89
00:04:03.750 --> 00:04:05.730
and expect the unexpected.

90
00:04:05.730 --> 00:04:07.670
There's not a reference for this.

91
00:04:07.670 --> 00:04:10.080
And we wanted to help turn this dream

92
00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:11.550
into reality and spread the love.

93
00:04:11.550 --> 00:04:15.210
So here to join us is Catherine Oliveros

94
00:04:15.210 --> 00:04:16.510
the Vice President

95
00:04:16.510 --> 00:04:18.310
